verywhere on $D.$*\n\nFor the vector field $F,$ we have $P=ay-2x{y}^{3}$ and $Q=x-3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=a-6x{y}^{2},\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=1-6x{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIt's clear that the partial derivatives exist and are continuous on ${R}^{2}.$ Equating the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a-6x{y}^{2} & =1-6x{y}^{2} \\\\ a & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $a=1.$" 13194139534992 true] [17592186325395 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325396 13194139534992 true] [17592186325395 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325397 13194139534992 true] [17592186325395 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325398 13194139534992 true] [17592186325395 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325399 13194139534992 true] [17592186325395 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325400 13194139534992 true] [17592186325395 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534992 true] [17592186325395 1041 "selection" 13194139534992 true] [17592186325395 1104 #edb/ref 17592186325398 13194139534992 true] [17592186325395 1110 #uuid "b5459ad7-120f-5776-8a41-d80a255496bb" 13194139534992 true] [17592186325396 1034 "-\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139534992 true] [17592186325396 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534992 true] [17592186325396 1111 #uuid "d299bc15-4ce0-5f6b-be6d-41a32a83e359" 13194139534992 true] [17592186325397 1034 "3" 13194139534992 true] [17592186325397 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534992 true] [17592186325397 1111 #uuid "05a6edda-d0c6-5b5b-b771-8880c54ba809" 13194139534992 true] [17592186325398 1034 "1" 13194139534992 true] [17592186325398 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534992 true] [17592186325398 1111 #uuid "c9b62821-566c-5ae9-89aa-0d7eadcf8cea" 13194139534992 true] [17592186325399 1034 "\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139534992 true] [17592186325399 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534992 true] [17592186325399 1111 #uuid "7be0721c-9ca8-59fa-a7e6-c4f261be1220" 13194139534992 true] [17592186325400 1034 "-2" 13194139534992 true] [17592186325400 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534992 true] [17592186325400 1111 #uuid "ad634012-1a47-55a6-9e0f-5e8e634cb31b" 13194139534992 true] [17592186325401 1017 #edb/ref 17592186325402 13194139534992 true] [17592186325401 1089 "q-104414" 13194139534992 true] [17592186325401 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534992 true] [17592186325401 1100 "Consider the vector field $F=\\frac{axy}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,i+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)\\,j$ on ${R}^{2},$ where $a$ is a constant. Given that $F$ is conservative, find the value of $a.$" 13194139534992 true] [17592186325401 1113 #uuid "d8ed3b7d-22fa-58ba-a534-22239fadeef6" 13194139534992 true] [17592186325401 1145 "Let $F(x,y)=P(x,y)\\,i+Q(x,y)\\,j$ be a vector field with domain $D={R}^{2},$ where $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first-order partial derivatives everywhere on $D.$ Then, we have the following theorem:\n\n$F$ *is conservative if and only if $\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}$ everywhere on $D.$*\n\nFor the vector field $F,$ we have $P=\\frac{axy}{{x}^{2}+1}$ and $Q=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1).$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{ax}{{x}^{2}+1},\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+1}.\n$$\n\nIt's clear that the partial derivatives exist and are continuous on ${R}^{2}.$ Equating the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{ax}{{x}^{2}+1} & =\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+1} \\\\ ax & =2x \\\\ a & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $a=2.$" 13194139534992 true] [17592186325402 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325403 13194139534992 true] [17592186325402 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325404 13194139534992 true] [17592186325402 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325405 13194139534992 true] [17592186325402 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325406 13194139534992 true] [17592186325402 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325407 13194139534992 true] [17592186325402 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534992 true] [17592186325402 1041 "selection" 13194139534992 true] [17592186325402 1104 #edb/ref 17592186325404 13194139534992 true] [17592186325402 1110 #uuid "dbd07589-35